          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: A witness sends us one of his photographs on which he is surprised to notice the presence of an element he did not see at the time of the shot. This photo without direct observation, which contains a gray streak following a bright point, is likely the result of an object passing very close to the lens very quickly. Indeed, this object is very blurry. It is probably an insect illuminated for an instant by the camera flash (the auxiliary EXIF data indicates that the flash was triggered). This case is classified as \"B\": probable photograph of an insect, with flash.",
